28","committee":"Governance Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-07","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-02","committee":"Finance and Performance Policy and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-04","committee":"Communities and Place Policy and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-18","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-25","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-09","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-03","committee":"Finance and Performance Policy and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Communities and Place Policy and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Communities and Place Policy and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Horsham faces \u00a31m budget shortfall by 2028 as government support grant ends","lead":"Horsham Council projected a \u00a31 million budget deficit by 2028/29 when a one-year government support grant expires, its Audit Committee heard on 16 September. The deficit reflects a combination of reduced central government funding and only 0.1 per cent assumed growth in the council's income. The council has already flagged a likely deficit in 2027/28 following the final government spending settlement, which reduced its core spending power by 4.3 per cent. The council balanced its 2026/27 budget only through use of the temporary support grant. Officials noted that a local government reorganisation scheduled by 2029 may mean Horsham will not need to deliver the savings required, but the structural funding gap is real and will require a financial plan if the council remains as currently configured.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"HDC Annex A 2026-27 Q1 progress_","paper_url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s34786/34786.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Governance Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 4 - Budget and Precept Calculations","paper_url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35028/35028.pdf","headline":"Reorganized authority anticipated to hold \u00a3210,000 reserves at 31 March 2027, sourced from NHPC reserves","detail":"The budget projects opening reserves of \u00a3210,000 at the end of the first financial year of the reorganized authority, drawn from North Horsham Parish Council reserves. This represents the balance sheet position post-merger and forms the financial cushion for the new combined entity.","category":"reserves","matters":"Reserve position indicates financial resilience and buffer for unforeseen costs or revenue shortfalls; material for assessing creditworthiness and financial sustainability post-reorganization","figures":"\u00a3210,000 anticipated reserves at 31/03/27","quote":"Anticipated reserve ~ 31/03/27 210,000.00\u00a3 From NHPC reserves","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Governance Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 4 - Budget and Precept Calculations","paper_url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35028/35028.pdf","headline":"Administrative and professional services costs doubled across the board for 'increased electorate' without quantifying growth","detail":"Multiple administrative line items double from 2026/27 to 2027/28 with the notation 'Doubled to account for increased electorate, and 5% increase'. These include insurance (\u00a316,500\u2192\u00a334,650), subscriptions (\u00a33,800\u2192\u00a37,980), external audit (\u00a31,500\u2192\u00a33,150), professional services (\u00a34,250\u2192\u00a38,925), and others. The paper does not quantify electorate growth or provide baseline comparisons.","category":"other","matters":"Doubling of administrative costs requires understanding whether driven by genuine electorate growth or administrative expansion; lenders assess budget robustness and inflation assumptions","figures":"Insurance \u00a316,500\u2192\u00a334,650, Subscriptions \u00a33,800\u2192\u00a37,980, External Audit \u00a31,500\u2192\u00a33,150, Professional Services \u00a34,250\u2192\u00a38,925","quote":"Doubled to account for increased electorate, and 5% increase","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Governance Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 4 - Budget and Precept Calculations","paper_url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35028/35028.pdf","headline":"Neighbourhood warden service expanded by 2 additional FTE, budget doubling from \u00a398,300 to \u00a3202,498","detail":"Neighbourhood warden costs more than double from \u00a398,300 to \u00a3202,498, with the budget paper explicitly stating 'provision for 2 additional wardens' beyond current staffing. This represents a significant service expansion and staffing commitment, though the paper does not explain the demand or policy driver.","category":"demand","matters":"Service expansion signals policy commitment or demand increase; lenders assess whether recurring spending commitments are justified and sustainable","figures":"\u00a398,300 to \u00a3202,498 (106% increase); 2 additional warden FTE","quote":"Neighbourhood wardens 98,300.00\u00a3 202,498.00\u00a3 3% increase staff costs, plus provision for 2 additional wardens","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Governance Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 4 - Budget and Precept Calculations","paper_url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35028/35028.pdf","headline":"Roffey Parish Council precept declining 36.31% post-reorganization with no explanation provided","detail":"Different areas of the reorganized authority face sharply divergent precept impacts. RPC residents face a Band D reduction of \u00a326.89 (36.31% decline) with no explanation in the paper. HTC residents face a 15.54% reduction (\u00a38.68 Band D) attributed to withdrawal of the special charge under review. NHPC residents see a modest 3.13% increase (\u00a31.43 Band D). The unexplained RPC decline raises questions about service provision or financial arrangements.","category":"governance","matters":"Uneven precept impacts across merged areas signal resource redistribution and potential merger tensions; unexplained 36% reduction warrants scrutiny of whether services are being reduced or funded differently","figures":"RPC -36.31% (\u00a326.89 Band D), HTC -15.54% (\u00a38.68 Band D), NHPC +3.13% (\u00a31.43 Band D)","quote":"% increase for RPC residents -36.31%","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Governance Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 4 - Budget and Precept Calculations","paper_url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35028/35028.pdf","headline":"Youth work budget increases 900% from \u00a36,000 to \u00a360,000 with only 'increased provision' cited","detail":"Youth work expenditure is budgeted to increase tenfold from \u00a36,000 in 2026/27 to \u00a360,000 in 2027/28. The only explanation provided in the budget paper is the notation 'Increased provision', with no detail on demand drivers, service specification, outcomes, or justification for this commitment.","category":"demand","matters":"Unexplained service commitments of this magnitude signal uncertain budget planning; lenders assess whether recurring spending is sustainable and grounded in genuine demand","figures":"\u00a36,000 to \u00a360,000 (900% increase)","quote":"Youth Work 6,000.00\u00a3 60,000.00\u00a3 Increased provision","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-16"},"name":"Horsham","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-26","since_iso":"2026-08-27","distress":false,"headline":"Month 4 \u00a30.44m surplus masked by one-off development income; underlying pressure from lost parking revenue and increased agency costs","lead":"Short-term surplus relies on one-off gains; underlying structural pressure toward deficit; strategy of reserve drawdown for non-revenue-generating purposes is unsustainable and contributes to the \u00a31m deficit risk by 2028/29.","also":["29 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Governance Committee on 2026-09-28","n_findings":30,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix A Corporate Risk Register Month 5 2026-27","top_paper_url":"https://horsham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s34920/34920.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":110,"news_drafts_total":1}}